WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.137
How do you know tenant restrictions work?

2
00:00:02.137 --> 00:00:06.425
Learn's four-case test, run from
a pilot device with the client on.

3
00:00:06.425 --> 00:00:09.875
A member of the agency's own
tenant signs in normally.

4
00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:12.775
An account from an allowed
partner tenant signs in.

5
00:00:12.775 --> 00:00:15.911
An account from a tenant that
isn't allowed is blocked,

6
00:00:15.911 --> 00:00:20.187
and Learn's block query finds it by
error five million two hundred eleven.

7
00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:23.563
And a guest in the agency's
tenant isn't evaluated.

8
00:00:23.563 --> 00:00:25.137
Record each outcome.

9
00:00:25.137 --> 00:00:26.737
Now, where are agencies?

10
00:00:26.737 --> 00:00:32.238
Both features come with Entra I D P one or
P two and the Microsoft traffic profile,

11
00:00:32.238 --> 00:00:33.988
are generally available,

12
00:00:33.988 --> 00:00:37.988
and are available in G C C by
Learn's product-wide statement.

13
00:00:37.988 --> 00:00:41.277
Where the Microsoft traffic
profile isn't adopted yet,

14
00:00:41.277 --> 00:00:44.859
the interim path is named-location
Conditional Access and

15
00:00:44.859 --> 00:00:48.650
device-side tenant restrictions
version two by Group Policy.
